WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.323 --> 00:00:04.171
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.171 --> 00:00:05.979
I started the Mentor Me series

00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:09.312
to try to hang around people
who've done a lot more than us

00:00:09.312 --> 00:00:11.872
and hopefully by spending a
little bit more time with them

00:00:11.872 --> 00:00:14.156
some of how they think,
their values, their beliefs,

00:00:14.156 --> 00:00:17.170
their mindsets, their
attitudes, seeps into us

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.963
to help us become the
best version of ourselves.

00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:22.034
So today we're going to
look at the Dalai Lama

00:00:22.034 --> 00:00:24.485
and some of his most inspiring speeches.

00:00:24.485 --> 00:00:25.949
Mentor me, Dalai Lama.

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:27.201
And as always guys, as you're watching

00:00:27.201 --> 00:00:29.709
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:29.709 --> 00:00:31.183
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:32.209
put quotes around it

00:00:32.209 --> 00:00:33.929
so other people can be inspired as well,

00:00:33.929 --> 00:00:35.324
and when you write it down

00:00:35.324 --> 00:00:38.818
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:38.818 --> 00:00:39.651
Enjoy.

00:00:39.651 --> 00:00:42.568
(inspiring music)*

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:55.789
(mystical music)

00:01:01.486 --> 00:01:04.689
- [Narrator] His Holiness
the 14th Dali Lama

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:07.052
is the spiritual and temporal leader

00:01:07.052 --> 00:01:10.385
of Tibet's people and exiled government.

00:01:11.388 --> 00:01:14.971
In 1959, he dramatically
escaped into exile

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:20.013
and established the Tibetan
government in northern India.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:23.096
The Dalai Lama has dedicated his life

00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:26.358
to the promotion of world peace.

00:01:26.358 --> 00:01:30.525
To this end, he was awarded
the Nobel Peace Prize in 1989.

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:37.084
Religious harmony and the
preservation of Tibetan culture

00:01:37.084 --> 00:01:39.917
are also two of his main concerns.

00:01:41.046 --> 00:01:43.373
(chanting)

00:01:43.373 --> 00:01:45.366
Throughout the last 50 years

00:01:45.366 --> 00:01:47.421
he has traveled around the world

00:01:47.421 --> 00:01:50.921
sharing his wisdom and Buddhist teachings.

00:01:52.398 --> 00:01:53.813
- [Woman In Audience] We love you!

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:57.063
- Thank you.
(laughter)

00:02:22.758 --> 00:02:23.813
- [Interviewer] In your experience,

00:02:23.813 --> 00:02:26.063
what makes you truly happy?

00:03:43.373 --> 00:03:45.040
What is human value?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:47.913
Money?

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.737
Oh yes, very important.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:57.843
Sometimes I jokingly to
telling Buddhist audiences,

00:03:57.843 --> 00:04:00.089
particularly Tibetan.

00:04:00.089 --> 00:04:02.506
We usually recite one Tibetan

00:04:04.356 --> 00:04:06.115
special sort of mantra.

00:04:06.115 --> 00:04:08.641
That is, Om Mani Padme Hum.

00:04:08.641 --> 00:04:12.808
So we recite and sometimes
in a little bit of hurry.

00:04:14.039 --> 00:04:17.139
Then we recite, "Om mani
padme hum, om mani padme hum."

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:20.349
Then, "Om mani, om
mani, mani, mani, mani."

00:04:20.349 --> 00:04:21.948
(audience laughs)

00:04:21.948 --> 00:04:26.364
So that sound looks like,
"Money, money, money, money."

00:04:26.364 --> 00:04:29.197
(audience laughs)

00:04:34.381 --> 00:04:37.846
So maybe, dollar, money, dollar, money

00:04:37.846 --> 00:04:42.013
or pound money, pound
money like that (laughs).

00:04:43.506 --> 00:04:46.839
So money, of course, what I think value,

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.457
and of course all these
external facilities.

00:04:52.941 --> 00:04:55.833
Those are valuable things, good.

00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:59.083
But all these provide physical comfort,

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.343
not mental comfort.

00:05:07.068 --> 00:05:08.758
If you have plenty of money,

00:05:08.758 --> 00:05:10.464
then some kind of satisfaction

00:05:10.464 --> 00:05:13.669
in the mental, "Oh, I
have a lot of money."

00:05:13.669 --> 00:05:15.463
That is illusion.

00:05:15.463 --> 00:05:19.380
Actually because we notice
about a billionaire,

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.215
plenty of money, but as a person,

00:05:25.215 --> 00:05:27.514
very unhappy person.

00:05:27.514 --> 00:05:29.382
Lot of worry.

00:05:29.382 --> 00:05:30.927
Lot of anxiety.

00:05:30.927 --> 00:05:32.982
Lot of suspicion.

00:05:32.982 --> 00:05:35.315
Lot of jealousy as a person.

00:05:36.448 --> 00:05:39.948
A billion money fail to bring inner peace.

00:05:41.237 --> 00:05:44.320
A billion money bring more suspicion,

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.860
more uncomfortable, more worry.

00:05:49.056 --> 00:05:53.253
Anyone who truly believe if you have money

00:05:53.253 --> 00:05:55.656
everything can solve.

00:05:55.656 --> 00:05:59.451
Everything can get real 100% satisfaction.

00:05:59.451 --> 00:06:01.714
That's, I think, an illusion.

00:06:01.714 --> 00:06:04.695
Money can bring some friend,

00:06:04.695 --> 00:06:07.459
but essentially, a friend of money,

00:06:07.459 --> 00:06:09.876
not friend of being yourself.

00:06:11.225 --> 00:06:13.071
Your fortune go like that.

00:06:13.071 --> 00:06:14.882
You become richer, richer, richer,

00:06:14.882 --> 00:06:16.799
you found more friends.

00:06:18.083 --> 00:06:20.833
When your fortune goes like that,

00:06:24.095 --> 00:06:27.762
then these friends also,
I think, disappear.

00:06:28.814 --> 00:06:30.538
Even when you want to telephone,

00:06:30.538 --> 00:06:32.205
they may not answer.

00:06:33.917 --> 00:06:37.774
So these friend are not
genuinely your friend,

00:06:37.774 --> 00:06:41.362
but a friend of your money (laughs).

00:06:41.362 --> 00:06:45.420
As I mentioned earlier, that is challenge.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.920
That's best opportunity to carry your way,

00:06:52.713 --> 00:06:55.296
your wisdom, your intelligence.

00:06:56.339 --> 00:07:00.506
If there's no challenge,
potential is over-relaxed.

00:07:03.183 --> 00:07:05.725
If challenge comes, then these potentials

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.415
become more alert.

00:07:07.415 --> 00:07:10.082
As a practitioner, as a Buddhist

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:15.117
my daily plan, right from
the beginning, early morning.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.873
These days about three, 3:30, I wake up.

00:07:23.027 --> 00:07:26.649
Then immediately I settle my mind,

00:07:26.649 --> 00:07:29.262
and the rest of the day, my body,

00:07:29.262 --> 00:07:33.179
speech, mind, dedicate
to well-being of others.

00:07:35.196 --> 00:07:38.279
Well that, so then more difficulties,

00:07:39.693 --> 00:07:44.117
more heavier responsibility,
have the subversity.

00:07:44.117 --> 00:07:47.950
Feel this good opportunity
to serve something.

00:07:50.072 --> 00:07:52.998
Write that as I mention it again.

00:07:52.998 --> 00:07:57.165
When you feel some problem,
and due to impatience,

00:07:58.519 --> 00:08:02.976
and due to short-sighted,
and due to narrow-minded

00:08:02.976 --> 00:08:05.059
then frustrations, anger.

00:08:08.149 --> 00:08:09.698
Better face problem.

00:08:09.698 --> 00:08:13.865
Look right away long time,
it brings more determination,

00:08:15.106 --> 00:08:16.786
more willpower.

00:08:16.786 --> 00:08:19.468
In order to keep inner-peace,

00:08:19.468 --> 00:08:22.468
compassion really makes differences.

00:08:23.561 --> 00:08:27.144
Very important because
self-centered person

00:08:29.429 --> 00:08:33.505
very certain to cherish
oneself, only oneself.

00:08:33.505 --> 00:08:36.517
So the reflection of that feeling,

00:08:36.517 --> 00:08:39.100
use word, "I, I, I," like that.

00:08:40.523 --> 00:08:44.859
So that word, nothing wrong,
but the real attitude here,

00:08:44.859 --> 00:08:46.810
and just think of oneself.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.560
So take only oneself,

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:53.810
then even tiny problem appears unbearable.

00:08:55.791 --> 00:08:59.208
If your attitude think others well-being,

00:09:00.057 --> 00:09:02.057
then others is infinite.

00:09:03.349 --> 00:09:06.135
So think more of others well-being,

00:09:06.135 --> 00:09:08.135
your mind open, widened.

00:09:10.297 --> 00:09:12.910
Then your own problem appears

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.493
not significant, insignificant.

00:09:17.611 --> 00:09:20.361
Same problem, same tragedy can be

00:09:21.722 --> 00:09:24.222
much different how you see it.

00:09:25.553 --> 00:09:29.907
This angle, you can
see something very bad.

00:09:29.907 --> 00:09:32.074
From this angle, oh, okay.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.960
That often, you see, happens;

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.127
therefore, the compassionate
attitude really widens.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:47.009
So one small problem, then
not much sort of seriousness.

00:09:47.009 --> 00:09:49.926
So that's I think make differences.

00:10:55.208 --> 00:10:58.125
Then aged 24 I lost my own country.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:02.330
It last 50 years now.

00:11:03.172 --> 00:11:06.589
Still a lot of problem, a lot of sadness,

00:11:07.815 --> 00:11:10.232
a lot of heart-breaking news.

00:11:11.533 --> 00:11:15.033
During this period, money failed to bring.

00:11:21.343 --> 00:11:22.858
(speaking foreign language)

00:11:22.858 --> 00:11:24.095
- [Man] Consolation.

00:11:24.095 --> 00:11:25.662
- Consolation.

00:11:25.662 --> 00:11:29.245
But then only thing
which bring inner-peace

00:11:31.197 --> 00:11:34.030
is my own inner-value, compassion,

00:11:39.019 --> 00:11:41.352
and a spirit of forgiveness,

00:11:43.082 --> 00:11:45.415
and also realistic attitude.

00:11:48.028 --> 00:11:51.778
These things brings
inner comfort more clear.

00:11:54.645 --> 00:11:57.673
and my physical health also.

00:11:57.673 --> 00:12:01.256
These inner-value really
affect positively.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:07.537
- [Man] On my health.

00:12:07.537 --> 00:12:08.370
- Ah?

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:09.216
- On my health.

00:12:09.216 --> 00:12:10.049
- On my?

00:12:10.049 --> 00:12:10.882
- Health.

00:12:10.882 --> 00:12:11.715
- Health.

00:12:11.715 --> 00:12:16.259
One specialist described
me as a young patient.

00:12:16.259 --> 00:12:19.259
Then I told him, "I'm not young, no.

00:12:21.195 --> 00:12:22.778
"Over 73 years old"

00:12:23.946 --> 00:12:27.529
So then he says, "Yes,
I know your age, 73,

00:12:30.721 --> 00:12:34.638
"but your body still
looks like a 60-year-old."

00:12:37.356 --> 00:12:40.575
So he described as a young patient.

00:12:40.575 --> 00:12:43.408
(audience laughs)

00:12:47.045 --> 00:12:50.878
So that shows my mental
peace, inner-strength.

00:12:56.327 --> 00:12:59.183
I think it really makes differences

00:12:59.183 --> 00:13:00.766
about body element.

00:13:02.004 --> 00:13:04.754
So we are same, same human being.

00:13:09.075 --> 00:13:12.825
Therefore I want to
share you ultimate source

00:13:13.688 --> 00:13:16.938
of your happy life, happy mental state.

00:13:19.454 --> 00:13:21.287
It is within yourself.

00:13:22.937 --> 00:13:24.817
That I think you should know.

00:13:24.817 --> 00:13:28.317
Then I think the best method to avoid fear

00:13:30.025 --> 00:13:32.359
or regret at the time of death

00:13:32.359 --> 00:13:34.192
is while we are alive.

00:13:35.372 --> 00:13:39.539
Our time, our energy must
utilized in a meaningful way.

00:13:42.947 --> 00:13:46.197
Serving others that's the most profound

00:13:51.339 --> 00:13:53.172
meaning of usefulness.

00:13:55.869 --> 00:13:59.452
Once in survival, even
animals also can do.

00:14:04.985 --> 00:14:07.615
But for service to other,

00:14:07.615 --> 00:14:10.782
is something unique about human being.

00:14:12.123 --> 00:14:16.290
I think bonding, the mother
and child, or offspring...

00:14:19.109 --> 00:14:19.942
- [Man] The bond.

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:22.938
The bond between mother
and, you want to say?

00:14:22.938 --> 00:14:26.266
- Even other animals also have.

00:14:26.266 --> 00:14:29.035
But they're, that kind
of closeness feeling

00:14:29.035 --> 00:14:30.742
should be it.

00:14:30.742 --> 00:14:33.877
But we, human being,
because of intelligence,

00:14:33.877 --> 00:14:37.739
that kind of feeling we
can prolong all out life.

00:14:37.739 --> 00:14:39.993
- [Man] Yeah, extend it through our life.

00:14:39.993 --> 00:14:44.160
- Some serving other people,
helping other people,

00:14:45.181 --> 00:14:49.484
is the, I think, very very
appropriate sort of action

00:14:49.484 --> 00:14:51.697
according to our intellect, correct?

00:14:51.697 --> 00:14:53.354
Or human ability.

00:14:53.354 --> 00:14:55.496
We have such an ability.

00:14:55.496 --> 00:14:59.536
So to utilize that ability, how say that?

00:14:59.536 --> 00:15:00.947
- [Man] In the most appropriate way.

00:15:00.947 --> 00:15:04.288
- Oh, appropriate way
is serving other people.

00:15:04.288 --> 00:15:07.205
Then at the end you feel no regret.

00:15:09.306 --> 00:15:12.306
I've done my best, something useful,

00:15:14.217 --> 00:15:15.887
something meaningful life.

00:15:15.887 --> 00:15:19.970
Now end come, although
sorry, sad, but no regret.

00:15:36.196 --> 00:15:37.955
- [Narrator] And yet, we have been told

00:15:37.955 --> 00:15:40.428
to fear anyone and everyone.

00:15:40.428 --> 00:15:43.109
A reality, he says, that is impacting

00:15:43.109 --> 00:15:46.692
one of the fundamentals
of human happiness.

00:16:36.474 --> 00:16:37.800
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.106
I hope you enjoyed it.

00:16:39.106 --> 00:16:41.144
I'd love to know what
you take from this video

00:16:41.144 --> 00:16:44.017
that you're going to
immediately apply to your life

00:16:44.017 --> 00:16:45.008
or to your business?

00:16:45.008 --> 00:16:47.288
What was the most important
lesson that you learned?

00:16:47.288 --> 00:16:48.772
Please leave it in the
comments down below,

00:16:48.772 --> 00:16:50.112
I'm super curious to find out.

00:16:50.112 --> 00:16:52.362
I also want to give a quick
shout out to John Sonmez,

00:16:52.362 --> 00:16:54.744
the Simple Programmer,
John thank you so much

00:16:54.744 --> 00:16:56.559
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word,

00:16:56.559 --> 00:16:58.995
and doing that awesome review
on your YouTube channel.

00:16:58.995 --> 00:17:00.947
I really really really appreciate it.

00:17:00.947 --> 00:17:02.445
- It's a good book,
definitely check it out.

00:17:02.445 --> 00:17:06.729
It's called Your One
Word by Evan Carmichael,

00:17:06.729 --> 00:17:07.931
again, a fellow YouTuber.

00:17:07.931 --> 00:17:09.549
- So thank you guys again for watching.

00:17:09.549 --> 00:17:10.959
I believe in you.

00:17:10.959 --> 00:17:13.085
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:17:13.085 --> 00:17:14.897
and whatever your one word is.

00:17:14.897 --> 00:17:17.314
Much love, I'll see you soon.

